Drop the unused <pwd.h> include from goo/gfile.cc.

wasi-libc has no user database and so no <pwd.h>, making this a hard build failure.
Nothing in Poppler references getpwnam/getpwuid/struct passwd -- this is the only mention
of pwd.h in the tree -- so the include is stale and removing it is a no-op everywhere.

Upstreamable as-is; not a WASI-specific workaround.

diff --git a/goo/gfile.cc b/goo/gfile.cc
index 32e892b6..56f79313 100644
--- a/goo/gfile.cc
+++ b/goo/gfile.cc
@@ -43,7 +43,6 @@
 #    include <sys/stat.h>
 #    include <fcntl.h>
 #    include <cstring>
-#    include <pwd.h>
 #endif // _WIN32
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <limits>
